config BR2_PACKAGE_CADR_READOUT
	bool "cadr-readout"
	select BR2_PACKAGE_CADR_COMMON
	help
	  The readout: the program that prints the CADR's own memories.
	  The control store, the boot PROM, the scratchpads, the
	  pushdown buffer, the micro-stack, the dispatch memory and both
	  levels of the map are inside the fabric, and the console's
	  readout window is the only way out of them.

	  It halts the machine while it reads and starts it again
	  afterwards, so it is run when somebody wants to look. It is
	  not a daemon and has no init script.
